Fix: wrap the final call in try/except TypeError, fall back to Index(new_values, name=self.name). But for object dtype CFTimeIndex, does _with_infer get here? The traceback shows yes. But wait — for object dtype, the code in the try above uses `_validate_fill_value`, which for object Index does nothing? Then since arr.dtype == object and item is str (not tuple/dt64), it goes to casted = arr.dtype.type(item) — fine. Then final line fails on CFTimeIndex constructor.

Actually the known pandas fix (GH#47071, referenced in the comment!) was to catch errors. Implement:

```python
try:
    return self._constructor._with_infer(new_values, name=self.name)
except TypeError:
    # e.g. third-party subclass like xarray CFTimeIndex GH#47780
    return Index._with_infer(new_values, name=self.name)
```

Also check `delete`, `append` etc.? Focus on insert. Check for `Index._with_infer` existence - yes classmethod. Apply edit.

